From db941510532bd14af26789d91d945c0ca0f2d0c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mattromano <42412983+mattromano@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:06:21 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(audio): live pitch shift on the monitored guitar
 (semitones + cents)

LivePitchShifter: two-tap granular delay-line shifter with WSOLA splice
alignment (search spans one low-string period, earliest strong peak, parabolic
sub-sample refinement), so pitch is exact even on low E. ~10-15 ms added
latency on down-tunings, ~8 ms for cents-only, bit-exact passthrough at 0.

Runs in SourceChain right after input gain, so note detection, the gate and
the tone chain hear the shifted guitar; the tuner's raw ring gets the dry
signal through a mirror gate and getRawPitch undoes the ratio.

Control rides on setTonePolish({ pitch: { semitones, cents, windowMs } }) so the
0.2.9 IPC bridge needs no change; status is on getDeviceMetrics().livePitch.
Adds the live_pitch ctest and an offline listening renderer.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
